(1) syntactic criterion: P-occurrences with argument tuples
  Sep    named args [('x', 'z')]                                  FO-named: True  guards: fresh(y, A)
         dB args    [((0, 2), 3)]                                 FO-dB:    True  guard: loose(A) <= {0, 2}
  SepJ   named args [('u',)]                                      FO-named: True  guards: fresh(X,Y, A)
         dB args    [((0,), 3)]                                   FO-dB:    True  guard: loose(A) <= {0}
  EInd   named args [('y',), ('x',), ('x',)]                      FO-named: False guards: -
         dB args    [((0,), 2), ((0,), 1), ((0,), 1)]             FO-dB:    True  guard: implied by well-formedness
  Coll   named args [('x', 'y', 'A'), ('x', 'y', 'A')]            FO-named: True  guards: fresh(Y, A)
         dB args    [((1, 0, 2), 3), ((1, 0, 3), 4)]              FO-dB:    False guard: -
  ReplU  named args [('x', 'y', 'A'), ('x', 'y', 'A')]            FO-named: True  guards: fresh(Y, A)
         dB args    [((1, 0, 2), 3), ((1, 0, 3), 4)]              FO-dB:    False guard: -
  ReplS  named args [('x', 'y', 'A'), ('x', 'u', 'A'), ('x', 'y', 'A')] FO-named: False guards: -
         dB args    [((1, 0, 2), 3), ((2, 0, 3), 4), ((1, 0, 3), 4)] FO-dB:    False guard: -
  ReplJ  named args [('x', 'y'), ('x', 'u'), ('x', 'y')]          FO-named: False guards: -
         dB args    [((2, 1), 3), ((2, 0), 3), ((0, 1), 4)]       FO-dB:    False guard: -

(2) which P-occurrences does the FO lgg tie together?  (all pool pairs with (R); keyed by (N_i))
  Sep  (args ('x', 'z'))
     N=(False, False)         named blocks ((1,),)                dB blocks ((1,),)                pairs 1
     N=(False, True)          named blocks ((1,),)                dB blocks ((1,),)                pairs 1
     N=(True, False)          named blocks ((1,),)                dB blocks ((1,),)                pairs 8
     N=(True, True)           named blocks ((1,),)                dB blocks ((1,),)                pairs 97
  SepJ  (args ('u',))
     N=(False,)               named blocks ((1,),)                dB blocks ((1,),)                pairs 6
     N=(True,)                named blocks ((1,),)                dB blocks ((1,),)                pairs 104
  EInd  (args ('x',))
     N=(False,)               named blocks ((1, 2, 3),)           dB blocks ((1, 2, 3),)           pairs 6
     N=(True,)                named blocks ((1,), (2, 3))         dB blocks ((1, 2, 3),)           pairs 104
  Coll  (args ('x', 'y', 'A'))
     N=(False, False, False)  named blocks ((1, 2),)              dB blocks ((1, 2),)              pairs 1
     N=(False, True, False)   named blocks ((1, 2),)              dB blocks ((1, 2),)              pairs 1
     N=(False, True, True)    named blocks ((1, 2),)              dB blocks ((1,), (2,))           pairs 5
     N=(True, False, False)   named blocks ((1, 2),)              dB blocks ((1, 2),)              pairs 1
     N=(True, False, True)    named blocks ((1, 2),)              dB blocks ((1,), (2,))           pairs 3
     N=(True, True, False)    named blocks ((1, 2),)              dB blocks ((1, 2),)              pairs 33
     N=(True, True, True)     named blocks ((1, 2),)              dB blocks ((1,), (2,))           pairs 62
  ReplU  (args ('x', 'y', 'A'))
     N=(False, False, False)  named blocks ((1, 2),)              dB blocks ((1, 2),)              pairs 1
     N=(False, True, False)   named blocks ((1, 2),)              dB blocks ((1, 2),)              pairs 1
     N=(False, True, True)    named blocks ((1, 2),)              dB blocks ((1,), (2,))           pairs 5
     N=(True, False, False)   named blocks ((1, 2),)              dB blocks ((1, 2),)              pairs 1
     N=(True, False, True)    named blocks ((1, 2),)              dB blocks ((1,), (2,))           pairs 3
     N=(True, True, False)    named blocks ((1, 2),)              dB blocks ((1, 2),)              pairs 33
     N=(True, True, True)     named blocks ((1, 2),)              dB blocks ((1,), (2,))           pairs 62
  ReplS  (args ('x', 'y', 'A'))
     N=(False, False, False)  named blocks ((1, 2, 3),)           dB blocks ((1, 2, 3),)           pairs 1
     N=(False, True, False)   named blocks ((1, 3), (2,))         dB blocks ((1, 2, 3),)           pairs 1
     N=(False, True, True)    named blocks ((1, 3), (2,))         dB blocks ((1,), (2, 3))         pairs 5
     N=(True, False, False)   named blocks ((1, 2, 3),)           dB blocks ((1, 3), (2,))         pairs 1
     N=(True, False, True)    named blocks ((1, 2, 3),)           dB blocks ((1,), (2,), (3,))     pairs 3
     N=(True, True, False)    named blocks ((1, 3), (2,))         dB blocks ((1, 3), (2,))         pairs 33
     N=(True, True, True)     named blocks ((1, 3), (2,))         dB blocks ((1,), (2,), (3,))     pairs 62
  ReplJ  (args ('x', 'y'))
     N=(False, False)         named blocks ((1, 2, 3),)           dB blocks ((1, 2, 3),)           pairs 1
     N=(False, True)          named blocks ((1, 3), (2,))         dB blocks ((1, 3), (2,))         pairs 1
     N=(True, False)          named blocks ((1, 2, 3),)           dB blocks ((1, 2), (3,))         pairs 8
     N=(True, True)           named blocks ((1, 3), (2,))         dB blocks ((1,), (2,), (3,))     pairs 97

(3) explicit instances of the FO lgg that are NOT schema instances (falsity: hand proofs in notes.md)
  EInd   named data bodies x=x, ¬x∈a; lgg blocks ((1,), (2, 3))
       instance: (∀x0.(∀x1.(x1∈x0 → ¬x1=x1) → ∀x1.¬x1∈x0) → ∀x0.∀x1.¬x1∈x0)
       instance of the lgg: True; sentence: True; instance of the schema: False
  ReplJ  named data bodies x∈z, ¬x=a; lgg blocks ((1, 3), (2,))
       instance: (∀x0.∀x1.∀x2.((x1=x1 ∧ ¬x2=x2) → x1=x2) → ∀x0.∃x1.∀x2.(x2∈x1 ↔ ∃x3.(x3∈x0 ∧ x2=x2)))
       instance of the lgg: True; sentence: True; instance of the schema: False
  ReplJ  db    data bodies x∈z, ¬x=a; lgg blocks ((1,), (2,), (3,))
       instance: (∀x0.∀x1.∀x2.((¬∀x3.x3=x3 ∧ ¬∀x3.x3=x3) → x1=x2) → ∀x0.∃x1.∀x2.(x2∈x1 ↔ ∃x3.(x3∈x0 ∧ x2=x2)))
       instance of the lgg: True; sentence: True; instance of the schema: False
  Coll   db    data bodies y=x, ¬x=A; lgg blocks ((1,), (2,))
       instance: ∀x0.(∀x1.(x1∈x0 → ∃x2.x2=x2) → ∃x1.∀x2.(x2∈x0 → ∃x3.(x3∈x1 ∧ ¬∀x4.x4=x4)))
       instance of the lgg: True; sentence: True; instance of the schema: False
  ReplU  db    data bodies y=x, ¬x=A; lgg blocks ((1,), (2,))
       instance: ∀x0.(∀x1.(x1∈x0 → ∃!x2.x2=x1) → ∃x1.∀x2.(x2∈x0 → ∃x3.(x3∈x1 ∧ ¬∀x4.x4=x4)))
       instance of the lgg: True; sentence: True; instance of the schema: False
  ReplS  db    data bodies y=x, ¬x=A; lgg blocks ((1,), (2,), (3,))
       instance: ∀x0.(∀x1.(x1∈x0 → ∃x2.(x2=x1 ∧ ∀x3.(¬∀x4.x4=x4 → x3=x2))) → ∃x1.∀x2.(x2∈x0 → ∃x3.(x3∈x1 ∧ ¬∀x4.x4=x4)))
       instance of the lgg: True; sentence: True; instance of the schema: False
  Sep    named data bodies x∈z, ¬x=a; lgg blocks ((1,),)
       instance: ∀x0.∃x1.∀x2.(x2∈x1 ↔ (x2∈x0 ∧ ¬x2∈x1))
       instance of the lgg: True; sentence: True; instance of the schema: False
  Sep    db    data bodies x∈z, ¬x=a; lgg blocks ((1,),)
       instance: ∀x0.∃x1.∀x2.(x2∈x1 ↔ (x2∈x0 ∧ ¬x2∈x1))
       instance of the lgg: True; sentence: True; instance of the schema: False
  Coll   named data bodies y=x, ¬x=A; lgg blocks ((1, 2),)
       instance: ∀x0.(∀x1.(x1∈x0 → ∃x2.x2=Y) → ∃x1.∀x2.(x2∈x0 → ∃x3.(x3∈x1 ∧ x3=x1)))
       instance of the lgg: True; sentence: True; instance of the schema: False
  ReplS  named data bodies y=x, ¬x=A; lgg blocks ((1, 3), (2,))
       instance: ∀x0.(∀x1.(x1∈x0 → ∃x2.(x2=Y ∧ ∀x3.(¬x3=x3 → x3=x2))) → ∃x1.∀x2.(x2∈x0 → ∃x3.(x3∈x1 ∧ x3=x1)))
       instance of the lgg: True; sentence: True; instance of the schema: False

(3b) de Bruijn capture by index shift: Coll with phi(x,y) not mentioning A; the dB lgg ties both occurrences,
     but without the guard loose(A) <= {#0,#1} the index #2 means A at occurrence 1 and Y at occurrence 2
  lgg blocks ((1, 2),); instance ∀x0.(∀x1.(x1∈x0 → ∃x2.x2=x0) → ∃x1.∀x2.(x2∈x0 → ∃x3.(x3∈x1 ∧ x3=x1))); sentence True; schema instance False

(4) EInd in de Bruijn: instances of the FO pattern with well-formed results are exactly the EInd instances
  3000 random A with loose indices in {#0,#1}: well-formed instances 1051, of which EInd instances 1051; ill-formed 1949

(5) general only-if (Theorem B1): generic data phi1 = /\_i z_i=z_i, phi2 = ~phi1; set the lgg slots of one block
    to TOP and all others to BOT: the result is an instance of the lgg but not of the schema
  Sep    named single block (FO pattern)
  Sep    db    single block (FO pattern)
  SepJ   named single block (FO pattern)
  SepJ   db    single block (FO pattern)
  EInd   named blocks ((1,), (2, 3))         instance of lgg True, schema instance False
  EInd   db    single block (FO pattern)
  Coll   named single block (FO pattern)
  Coll   db    blocks ((1,), (2,))           instance of lgg True, schema instance False
  ReplU  named single block (FO pattern)
  ReplU  db    blocks ((1,), (2,))           instance of lgg True, schema instance False
  ReplS  named blocks ((1, 3), (2,))         instance of lgg True, schema instance False
  ReplS  db    blocks ((1,), (2,), (3,))     instance of lgg True, schema instance False
  ReplJ  named blocks ((1, 3), (2,))         instance of lgg True, schema instance False
  ReplJ  db    blocks ((1,), (2,), (3,))     instance of lgg True, schema instance False
